JaCoCo Coverage Plugin for Geany
=================================

This plugin adds a sidebar panel to Geany that displays a JaCoCo code
coverage report parsed from a standard JaCoCo CSV file (jacoco-report.csv).

Features
--------
* Package tree with expandable class nodes
* Coverage percentages for instructions, branches, lines, and methods
* Colour-coded values: green (≥80%), orange (≥50%), red (<50%)
* Aggregated package-level coverage rolled up from all classes
* Open any CSV via the toolbar file chooser
* Refresh button to reload the report without reopening the dialog

Usage
-----
1. Generate a JaCoCo CSV report from your build (e.g. Maven jacoco:report goal
   with the csvReport destination).  The default output is typically
   target/jacoco-report.csv or target/site/jacoco/jacoco.csv.
2. In Geany, switch to the "JaCoCo" sidebar tab.
3. Click the Open button and select the CSV file.
4. Expand package nodes to browse class-level coverage.
5. Click Refresh any time you regenerate the report.

CSV Format
----------
The plugin expects the standard JaCoCo CSV format:

    GROUP,PACKAGE,CLASS,
    INSTRUCTION_MISSED,INSTRUCTION_COVERED,
    BRANCH_MISSED,BRANCH_COVERED,
    LINE_MISSED,LINE_COVERED,
    COMPLEXITY_MISSED,COMPLEXITY_COVERED,
    METHOD_MISSED,METHOD_COVERED

